Follow-up to #1. README.md is hand-maintained (include_readme is off), so the POD change did not touch it.

The "Net::Async::MCP::Server::Transport::Stdio" section still says handle_requests blocks reading STDIN line by line until EOF. After #1 it still blocks the caller until EOF, but it reads through an IO::Async::Stream registered in the loop, so other notifiers keep running. The sentence should say that.

The section should also mention the two new public accessors, read_handle and write_handle (defaulting to STDIN and STDOUT), which are documented in POD but nowhere in README.

README.md also still declares version 0.001 while lib/ is at 0.002 - separate pre-existing drift, worth folding into the same pass.
